# Cursor rules — canonical repository redirect

This personal repository is a historical mirror, not the active source of truth. For all Berkah POS implementation, architecture, database, CI, security, deployment and release work, use [berkah-pos/Berkahtigaputeri](https://github.com/berkah-pos/Berkahtigaputeri).

Before active work, read the canonical [AGENTS.md](https://github.com/berkah-pos/Berkahtigaputeri/blob/main/AGENTS.md), [accepted owner ADR](https://github.com/berkah-pos/Berkahtigaputeri/blob/main/docs/permanent/ADR-2026-10-17-OWNER-KVM2-LARAVEL-POSTGRESQL-NO-SUPABASE.md), [DOC_00 configuration contract](https://github.com/berkah-pos/Berkahtigaputeri/blob/main/docs/permanent/DOC_00_CANONICAL_ARCHITECTURE_DECISION.md), [DOC_14 target architecture and acceptance gates](https://github.com/berkah-pos/Berkahtigaputeri/blob/main/docs/permanent/DOC_14_KVM2_ISOLATED_TENANT_ARCHITECTURE.md), and [master roadmap](https://github.com/berkah-pos/Berkahtigaputeri/blob/main/docs/permanent/DOC_00_MASTER_ROADMAP.md) in the organization repository.

The owner ADR selects the target platform; a decision is not proof of implementation or deployment. Verify current organization `main`, the exact candidate SHA, its relevant CI and direct staging/production evidence rather than relying on dated statements in this mirror.

Old code, SQL/RLS/RPC, workbook artifacts, scripts and reports in this personal mirror are historical/source-migration evidence, not current architecture authority. Preserve them unless an approved retention decision says otherwise. Do not run mutation-capable legacy scripts against unknown/shared resources.

Do not originate application or architecture changes here. Work in the organization repository on a dedicated branch and submit a reviewed PR.
